<title>AUSTRIA: Creditanstalt sees better full-year.</title>
<headline>Creditanstalt sees better full-year.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Creditanstalt-Bankverein, Austria's number two bank, reiterated on Friday it expected full-year net profit to exceed the 2.17 billion schillings reported for 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect a higher net profit,&quot; chief executive Guido Schmidt-Chiari said at an investment fair. He added loan loss provisions were expected to fall &quot;significantly&quot; below last year's 3.55 billion schillings.</p>
<p>Creditanstalt, which has topped the government's privatisation list for six years, is due to publish nine-month figures early next month.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
